From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: Add a driver for the Samsung S5K4H7 sensor

The S5K4H7 is an 8 MP raw sensor with a MIPI CCS register map. Some
Huawei MateBook E Go units carry it as their front camera (Xinli module)
instead of the Hynix HI846.

The power sequence, the init settings and the three modes (3264x2448,
3264x1836 and 1632x1224 binned, all 30 fps from a 280 MHz pixel clock,
four lanes at 350 MHz) are those of the module configuration that the
Windows camera driver ships for that module. The Bayer order, the
analogue gain range and the exposure limits come from the sensor's CCS
registers at probe. On that module they read GRBG, gain codes 32 to 512
with gain = code / 32, and an exposure of 2 lines up to the frame length
minus 4.

A board that may carry another module on the same connector describes
both, so a sensor that does not answer is reported at info level only
and the probe returns -ENODEV.

Tested on a MateBook E Go with the S5K4H7 module: preview and still
capture in Aperture and in another app.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
